+def expected_partners_for(date: str, leg: str, quantity: str) -> set:
+    """Sentinel 2 config (MDPF_ASSETS.019): the partners that MUST appear in the
+    cohort decomposition for a given as-of date -- DERIVED FROM THE ROSTER, never
+    restated here.
+
+    A partner is expected on `date` when the roster declares that (leg, quantity)
+    cell effective on that date: `effective_from <= date` and, when bounded,
+    `date <= effective_to`. `leg`/`quantity` are parameters because the roster is
+    keyed (firm, leg, quantity) and the cells genuinely differ -- cottonwood's
+    model.value starts 2026-05-28 while its model.count only starts 2026-07-22.
+
+    ⚠ A partner declared effective but ABSENT from the data is the caller's finding
+    to report. This function answers "who is EXPECTED", never "who showed up" -- the
+    two must not be derived from the same source, which is exactly the defect that
+    let `feeders_missing: []` be literally true while cottonwood was missing."""
